-- title:
--   Injectivity of substitution along ρ over a local Noetherian base
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative ring that is local and Noetherian, let $n$ be a natural number, and let $\rho = (\rho_i)_{i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,n}$ be a family of formal power series in $B[\![x_i : i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,n]\!]$ each of which has vanishing constant coefficient. Assume there is a natural number $N$ such that $X_i^N$ lies in the ideal generated by the set $\{\rho_i\}$ for every $i$, and assume the quotient of $B[\![x]\!]$ by that ideal is a finite $B$-module. Then for all power series $H, H' \in B[\![x]\!]$, the equality $\mathrm{subst}\,\rho\,H = \mathrm{subst}\,\rho\,H'$ of substitutions forces $H = H'$; that is, the substitution map $H \mapsto H(\rho_1, \dots, \rho_n)$ is injective on $B[\![x_1, \dots, x_n]\!]$. (The vanishing of the constant coefficients is what makes the substitution operation legitimate in the first place.)
--
--   This is the local Noetherian case of the statement that a finite substitution endomorphism of a power series ring, with infinitesimal and finite cokernel data as in the hypotheses, is injective; over a local base no projectivity assumption on the quotient is needed. It is used in the study of formal isogenies between fake elliptic curves arising in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd setting, where it rules out distinct formal parametrisations with the same composite.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPowerSeries_subst_injective_of_finite_quotient_of_X_pow_mem_span_of_isLocalRing.lean

